# Bina — Cursor Rules

## Project
Virtual science lab platform for Kenyan secondary school students.
Stack: React 18 + Vite (frontend) | FastAPI + SQLAlchemy (backend) | Supabase | Gemini Flash | Groq Llama 3.3

## Code style

### Python (backend)
- Python 3.11+, type hints on all functions
- async/await throughout — no sync DB calls
- Pydantic models for all request/response bodies
- SQLAlchemy async sessions only — use get_db() dependency
- All transactions explicit: wrap multi-table writes in one session, rollback on exception
- Never hardcode secrets — always use settings from config.py
- Logging: use Python logging module, never print()

### JavaScript/React (frontend)
- React 18 functional components only — no class components
- Hooks: useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef
- No direct API calls in components — use services/api.js
- Tailwind utility classes only — no inline style objects except in generated experiment components
- All interactive elements: minimum 44px touch target
- Focus rings on all interactive elements (focus-visible)

## Architecture rules
- NEVER store API keys in frontend code or git
- Generated JSX runs in sandboxed iframe only — never eval() in main window
- All DB writes that touch multiple tables go in one transaction
- Cache check before EVERY generation call — document_hash is the key
- Agent files live in backend/agents/ — one file per agent
- Keep components small: if > 150 lines, split it

## Naming
- Components: PascalCase
- Hooks: camelCase starting with 'use'
- API service functions: camelCase
- DB models: PascalCase
- Routes: kebab-case URLs

## What NOT to do
- No direct Supabase client calls from frontend pages — go through api.js
- No synchronous SQLAlchemy
- No console.log in committed code
- No purple gradients on white backgrounds (off-brand)
- No hardcoded experiment content — everything comes from documents
